title: "Lynxo: The Kadero Embedding — A Learnable Geometric Representation for Power-Network Criticality"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Berassil"
    given-names: "Abdelkader"
    affiliation: "University of Mustapha Stambouli, Mascara, Algeria"
date-released: 2026-08-17
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/dynaio/kadero-embedding"
url: "https://berassil-abdelkader.web.app"
keywords:
  - power systems
  - spectral graph theory
  - effective resistance
  - graph Laplacian
  - graph embeddings
  - electrical engineering
  - criticality analysis
  - contingency analysis
  - machine learning
abstract: >
  An independent research project proposing the Kadero Embedding: a
  differentiable, multi-channel high-dimensional vector-space
  representation of a power network, combining electrical, geographic,
  redundancy-structure, and operating-point information, each channel
  backed by a proof. Includes a complete mathematical foundation and an
  honestly-reported, self-correcting empirical validation program across
  IEEE 14-, 30-, 118-bus and a 300-bus test network. Archived openly for
  extension by the power-systems and applied-mathematics community.
